+codex
+I’ve confirmed two direct database bypasses with executable probes: a newly created subscription-built job can reach `done` with both review requirements at zero, and an unversioned research job can reach `done` because `NULL IS NULL` makes unversioned verdicts look version-matched. The live database is in WAL mode and connections now have an explicit 15-second lock wait; that prevents immediate lock failures but does not fix the remaining audit and finalization races.
